/-!
# Vertical orientation (T96)

Unicode's `Vertical_Orientation` property (UAX #50), reduced to the one
question usvg 0.48.1 asks of it: is a character `U` (upright)?  usvg's
`apply_writing_mode` stands exactly those clusters upright in vertical text
and turns every other one sideways, `Tu`/`Tr` included (`char_orientation(c)
== Orientation::Upright`).

The ranges are the `Upright` arms of the `unicode-vo` 0.1.0 crate usvg uses
(MIT/Apache-2.0, generated from `VerticalOrientation-17.txt`), adjacent ranges
merged; no arm of that table overlaps another with a different value, so the
merge is exact.  Everything else is `R`.
-/

namespace LeanSvg
namespace VertOrient

